{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.YekutieliLifting","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.YekutieliLifting","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.perpetual_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.perpetual_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L50-L70","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction**: if κ₀ is non-torsion, then κₙ ≠ 0 for all n.\n\n**Re-scoped 2026-11-15 (owner decision, PR #7747, bean `qou-lx8f`).**\nThis is a valid conditional: the conclusion holds whenever the\npersistence hypothesis does. It does not apply to the Kummer tower of\nBring's surface, where the obstruction vanishes for `n ∣ χ = -6` and\npersists only for `n ∤ 6`; the \"complementary subgroups\" argument for\npersistence there is withdrawn (item 3 of `thm:qu-to-qou` is now the\ndegree condition).\n\nThe key insight: κ₀ and the jet corrections at level n live in\ncomplementary subgroups of H²(S, B), so corrections cannot cancel κ₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.persistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.persistence","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Persistence: if κ₀ ≠ 0, then κₙ ≠ 0 for all n (jet corrections\nlive in a complementary subgroup, so cannot cancel κ₀). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.no_lift_of_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.no_lift_of_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Obstruction: if κₙ ≠ 0, no lift exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.lift_of_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.lift_of_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Lifting criterion: if κₙ = 0, the lift at level n exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.LiftType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.LiftType","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The type of lifts at level n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.kappa_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.kappa_zero","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L39-L39","doc":"The base-level obstruction κ₀ (the Euler class). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.kappa","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The obstruction class κₙ at level n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.deceq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.deceq","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L35-L35","doc":"Decidable equality on the obstruction space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.zero","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Zero element (trivial obstruction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.ObstructionSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.ObstructionSpace","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L31-L31","doc":"The obstruction space H²(S, B). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.YekutieliLifting","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.YekutieliLifting","kind":"structure","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.lean#L18-L48","doc":"**Yekutieli lifting in the brane tower**: each transition Aₙ ↪ A_{n+1}\ndefines a central extension of gerbes, and the Yekutieli lifting condition\nholds — the lift exists iff the obstruction class κₙ vanishes.\n\nBy [Theorem 4.17, yekutieli2010], any central extension of gerbes banded\nby an abelian sheaf satisfies this criterion.  The jet prolongation\nrealises each transition as precisely such an extension.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:yekutieli-lifting}`\nRef: [yekutieli2010] Theorem 4.17 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:yekutieli-lifting","label":"prop:yekutieli-lifting","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/yekutieli-lifting.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}